# Stream host test (test/m4/stream.sh): the OPEN seam t0a0c -> t0a0d
# (a1a2, cwg flags 8, the elevator). New Game on t0a0c; the player walks
# into the seam's approach box (t0a0d opens, its draw set lands), then
# stands in the elevator (the carry box) facing its back wall, where
# t0a0d's own elevator surfaces draw across layers (ren: oseam=). The
# shots `open-seam` and `open-seam-2` bracket a `set r_openseam` change
# the caller may make between them (stream.sh: none; the ares evidence
# run: 0 at frame 140, an A/B pair of the same pose).
# Syntax and semantics: docs/formats/route-bytecode.md.
startmap t0a0c
setpos -1100 -1508 40 0 0
wait 3
setpos -749 -1508 40 0 180
wait 1
shot open-seam
stats open-seam
wait 1
shot open-seam-2
pass
